bouncy-lang programs vendored for integration testing
=======================================================

`.in` files from the upstream bouncy-lang repo:

  https://github.com/Mercerenies/bouncy-lang
  copy is at internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/bouncy-lang/

each `.in` is `<name>.bn` from `examples/`. the `.expected` files
were generated by running goruby's evaluator directly (not MRI):

  go build -o bouncy_runner runner.go
  bouncy_runner <fixture>.in > <fixture>.expected

bouncy-lang uses ruby 3.0+ endless method syntax (def foo = expr),
which MRI 2.6.10 (the local baseline used for other gems) parses as
a syntax error. goruby's parser accepts the form; the resulting
output was hand-verified against the upstream README description
of each program's intended behaviour. when a ruby 3.x oracle is
available, the .expected files can be regen'd against it.

omitted programs and why
------------------------

- factorial.bn -- expects numeric stdin (n -> n!). under empty
  stdin both goruby and (hypothetical) mri error out without
  output, no useful baseline.
- truth_machine.bn -- expects 0 or 1 on stdin. same situation.

